<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lalitaditya Muktapida</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lalitaditya Muktapida was the most powerful king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karkota-dynasty">Karkota dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a>, ruling in the first half of the 8th century. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajatarangini">Kalhana's Rajatarangini</a> describes far-reaching campaigns, and he defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yashovarman-of-kannauj">Yashovarman of Kannauj</a>. He is credited with building the Sun temple at Martand, whose ruins still stand.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lalitaditya-muktapida.jpg" alt="Lalitaditya Muktapida" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shaurya · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Martanda_sun_temple.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
